      "timestamp_raw": "Apr 13, 2013 17:21:19 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "I just acquired this plant from Rob Co, and it looks completely different under his conditions.  Grown outdoors, it looks almost like S. flava 'Killer' with the intense, dark red throat.  I think this one originated from a Carolina flava cuprea that was crossed back with flava var. flava or a cuprea that was selfed:<br/><br/><a href=\"http://s1110.photobucket.com/user/meizzwang/media/April%202013/IMG_0087_zps85dbc7d6.jpg.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/April%202013/IMG_0087_zps85dbc7d6.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a><br/><br/><a href=\"http://s1110.photobucket.com/user/meizzwang/media/April%202013/IMG_0088_zps98a78608.jpg.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/April%202013/IMG_0088_zps98a78608.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a><br/><br/><a href=\"http://s1110.photobucket.com/user/meizzwang/media/April%202013/IMG_0040_zps948d8119.jpg.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/April%202013/IMG_0040_zps948d8119.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a><br/><br/><br/>Here's the same exact clone growing in Rob Co's greenhouse:<br/><a href=\"http://s1110.photobucket.com/user/meizzwang/media/April%202013/IMG_0007_zpsd698414c.jpg.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/April%202013/IMG_0007_zpsd698414c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a><br/><br/> ",
